  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/086B90">Definition <span data-tag="086B90">7.1.6.3</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos. According to Proposition <a href="/tag/A780C6" data-tag="A780C6">6.3.4.1</a>, there exists a geometric morphism $q_{\ast }: \calX \rightarrow \SSet $, which is unique up to homotopy. Let $q^{\ast }$ be a left adjoint to $q_{\ast }$ (also unique up to homotopy). The composition $q_{\ast } q^{\ast }: \SSet \rightarrow \SSet $ is an accessible left-exact functor, which we will refer to as the <em>shape of $\calX $</em> and denote by $Sh(\calX ) \in \Pro (\SSet )$. shape!of an $\infty $-toposShcalX@$Sh(\calX )$ </p>
